id:                     E6403
trigger_tool:           Conan|CI|network|wrapdb|download
phase:                  source-download|conan-create|ci-repair
error_signature:        wrapdb get_patch redirect to GitHub timeout while recipe-level download bypasses CI mirror rewrite
severity:               2
category:               build,network,conan,test-framework,evidence
match_keywords:         wrapdb.mesonbuild.com, get_patch, releases/download, ghproxy.net, Conan download, sha256, auxiliary input
title:                  WrapDB auxiliary patch URLs need deterministic mirror projection

root_cause:             The CI pre-download mirror transform covers URLs visible in conandata.yml only until it restores the official file. A recipe-level download() of a WrapDB get_patch endpoint then follows a redirect to GitHub and can time out on a restricted worker. The WrapDB endpoint exposes a deterministic release identifier, so the byte-equivalent release archive can be projected to an approved mirror without changing the canonical metadata.
affected_scope:        Conan recipes that acquire Meson WrapDB patches or other redirecting auxiliary inputs inside source(), after a disposable CI URL rewrite has been restored.
verification_cmd:      Derive the release URL only from the exact WrapDB endpoint shape; download it with Conan's normal hash-verified API; compare bytes and SHA-256 to the declared patch digest; retain the official endpoint as the final fallback and remove only a regular partial destination after failure.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           deterministic-wrapdb-release-mirror
rec_description:        Preserve the WrapDB URL, filename, and digest as canonical provenance. For an exact /v2/<release>/get_patch URL, try the corresponding mesonbuild/wrapdb release archive through one approved mirror, then the official endpoint. Never accept a proxy response without the declared SHA-256.
rec_command:            conan create <recipe> -pr:h <ohos-profile> -pr:b default --build=<package> with WrapDB release projection
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               bounded candidate generator shared by auxiliary framework downloads

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      official-wrapdb-endpoint
fallback_description:   The original WrapDB endpoint remains the authoritative fallback and must be attempted after the bounded mirror candidate; if both fail, source() fails closed.
fallback_command:       download the exact get_patch endpoint with the same SHA-256
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:           Conan download

forbid_1_pattern:       accept a redirect response or non-empty proxy body without SHA-256|infer archive identity from HTTP status
forbid_1_reason:        Redirect proxies can return HTML, truncated bytes, or a different release while reporting success.
forbid_1_consequence:   The test framework patch may be corrupted or non-reproducible and the failure can move from source acquisition into compilation.
forbid_2_pattern:       replace the canonical WrapDB URL with a personal mirror|allow arbitrary environment URLs
forbid_2_reason:        Provenance and the reproducible source contract become unverifiable.
forbid_2_consequence:   Future CI runs can consume an uncontrolled archive or fail repository source checks.

principles:             P005,P010,P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E6401]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

